# L20 environment setup

Use Python 3.10, UCM 0.3.0, vLLM 0.9.2, Torch 2.7.0/CUDA 12.6 and
Transformers 4.53.2. Driver 580 supports this CUDA runtime; keep the driver.
Run the blocks in order. These commands install/check the environment only.

## Update and activate

```bash
cd /data/jh/unified-cache-management
git fetch origin
git switch prophetkv/clean-qwen3-32b-yarn4
git pull --ff-only origin prophetkv/clean-qwen3-32b-yarn4
conda activate /data/jh/envs/ucm
export PYTHON_BIN=/data/jh/envs/ucm/bin/python
export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
```

## Dependencies

Ubuntu/Debian packages (use distribution equivalents elsewhere):

```bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y build-essential git pkg-config libnuma-dev libaio-dev
```

Install the toolkit separately, or point CUDA_HOME at an existing complete 12.6
toolkit. The CUDA version in nvidia-smi does not identify the installed toolkit.

```bash
conda create -y -p /data/jh/envs/cuda-12.6 -c nvidia 'cuda-toolkit=12.6'
export CUDA_HOME=/data/jh/envs/cuda-12.6
export PATH="$CUDA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
export CUDACXX="$CUDA_HOME/bin/nvcc"
nvcc --version

"$PYTHON_BIN" -m pip install --upgrade pip
"$PYTHON_BIN" -m pip install 'setuptools>=77,<80' wheel 'cmake==3.31.6' ninja 'wrapt==1.17.2'
"$PYTHON_BIN" -m pip install \
    'torch==2.7.0+cu126' 'torchvision==0.22.0+cu126' 'torchaudio==2.7.0+cu126' \
    --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126
"$PYTHON_BIN" -m pip install \
    'torch==2.7.0+cu126' 'vllm==0.9.2' 'transformers==4.53.2'

PLATFORM=cuda ENABLE_SPARSE=FALSE "$PYTHON_BIN" -m pip install -v \
    --no-build-isolation --no-deps --no-cache-dir --no-binary=uc-manager \
    'uc-manager==0.3.0'
```

UCM builds native storage/metrics libraries and downloads C++ dependencies.
The build-time sparse flag skips unrelated native extensions; this checkout
supplies ProphetKV's Python/Triton code. Do not install UCM 0.7.0 for this branch.

## Verify

```bash
"$PYTHON_BIN" -m pip check
PYTHONPATH="$PWD" CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' "$PYTHON_BIN" - <<'PY'
from importlib.metadata import version
for name, expected in {'torch': '2.7.0', 'vllm': '0.9.2',
                       'transformers': '4.53.2', 'uc-manager': '0.3.0'}.items():
    actual = version(name)
    assert actual.split('+')[0] == expected, (name, actual)
    print(name, actual)
import torch
import vllm._C
from ucm.store.pcstore import ucmpcstore
from ucm.shared.metrics import ucmmetrics
assert torch.version.cuda == '12.6'
print(ucmpcstore.__file__, ucmmetrics.__file__, sep='\n')
PY
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' "$PYTHON_BIN" -m unittest discover -s tests -v
"$PYTHON_BIN" -m pip freeze > /data/jh/envs/ucm/packages-installed.txt
```

Use `bash run.sh ...` for inference so private patches and runtime flags apply.
See README for model/input preparation and explicit GPU UUID selection. L20
inference validation is still required before accepting benchmark results.
